# GNATdoc annotations (host Ada)

Document Ada **specs** with [GNATdoc 4 annotations](https://docs.adacore.com/live/wave/gnatdoc4/html/gnatdoc-doc/annotations.html). Use **leading** comments (block immediately before the entity). Invoke with `--style=leading` (see `scripts/gnatdoc.ps1`).

Always document:

- **Packages** — comment immediately before `package … is`
- **Records** — type comment plus **`@field`** (and **`@disc`** for discriminants)
- **Enums** — type comment plus **`@enum`** for every literal
- **Subprograms** — comment plus **`@param`** for every parameter and **`@return`** for functions

Do **not** document fields, literals, or parameters with inline comments after the declaration. Put `@field`, `@enum`, `@param`, and `@return` in the leading block.

```ada
-- BAD
type Point is record
   X : Integer;  --  Horizontal
   Y : Integer;
end record;

function Compile (Pattern : String) return Regex_Result;
--  Compiles Pattern.

-- GOOD
--  Integer pixel location.
--  @field X Horizontal coordinate.
--  @field Y Vertical coordinate.
type Point is record
   X : Integer;
   Y : Integer;
end record;

--  Compile Pattern into an NFA.
--  @param Pattern UTF-8 regular-expression source.
--  @return Compiled engine, or a Regex_Error.
function Compile (Pattern : String) return Regex_Result;
```

Bodies do not replace spec docs. Nested helpers in bodies need no GNATdoc tags.
